## Reveal: add content on a click

Wrap anything in `<step>` and it stays hidden until the next click. Nothing moves when it appears:
the space is reserved.

<step>
  This text appeared on the first click.
</step>

<step>
  - and a list
  - on the second
</step>

<step>
  <code lang=typescript>
    const clicks = 3; // the code block came last
  </code>
</step>

<step>
  A list can appear bullet by bullet: write `<text steps>` around it.
</step>

<text steps>
  - first click
  - second click
  - third click
</text>

<notes>
  Works for text, lists, images, video, charts and code blocks. Frames of a code block count as clicks too. `<step at=3>` names the click.
</notes>
